%% Figure 2 — End-to-End Registration and Verification Data Flow
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant AW as Aid Worker<br/>(Register.jsx)
    participant CAM as Browser<br/>MediaPipe + Webcam
    participant API as FastAPI<br/>main.py
    participant JSON as JSON stores
    participant ALGO as Algorand<br/>RefugeeContract

    Note over AW,ALGO: Registration (custodial path)
    AW->>CAM: Run 5 liveness challenges
    CAM->>CAM: EAR + head pose<br/>composite SHA-256
    CAM-->>AW: personhood_hash (client)
    AW->>API: POST /api/blockchain/generate-custodial-wallet
    API->>ALGO: Fund W1, opt-in, register(H_ID, H_person, H_age)
    API->>JSON: Save .custodial-wallets.json + .registry.json
    API-->>AW: identity_id, W1 address, QR payload
    AW->>AW: Print RIMS Security Card (QR)

    Note over AW,ALGO: Verification / aid (online)
    AW->>API: GET /api/blockchain/refugee-state/{address}
    API->>ALGO: Read local state
    ALGO-->>API: hashes, aid_claimed
    API-->>AW: On-chain status
    AW->>API: POST /api/blockchain/claim-aid
    API->>ALGO: claim_aid(refugee)
    ALGO-->>API: aid_claimed = 1
